# --- ReviewGate-R execution-model study (analysis/syncasync) ---
# The read-only seed DB is rebuilt byte-identically by build_db.py and its
# sha256 is recorded in the pre-registration, so the binary is not tracked.
# Smoke cell output is provenance only and is never analysed.
analysis/syncasync/results/reviewgate_ro.db
analysis/syncasync/results/cells/
analysis/syncasync/results/smoke/
analysis/syncasync/results/main/
# Single-probe smoke knees: throwaway rates, provenance only.
analysis/syncasync/results/smoke_knees/
# Per-host topology cache. Machine-specific (core count, sibling groups, which
# siblings are offlined) and captured on the box by prepare_box.py, so a copy
# from another machine would silently misreport the pinning layout.
analysis/syncasync/results/topology.json

analysis/novelty/out/novelty_repo_context.json

# --- R=40 experiment raw artifacts (2026-09-28) ---
# The per-request k6 output and the knee ramp CSVs are 21GB / 260MB. The
# run-level aggregates they reduce to ARE tracked, so the analysis is
# reproducible from the repo without the raw per-request dumps.
analysis/out/experiment/standalone_R40/knee_A.csv
analysis/out/experiment/standalone_R40/knee_B.csv
analysis/out/experiment/standalone_R40/steady/
analysis/experiment/results/steady/

# 3.1GB per-request dump for the two failing A.480 cells; the diagnosis
# derived from it is in A480_failure_diagnosis.md, which IS tracked.
analysis/out/experiment/standalone_R40/raw_A480_failing/

# --- Tier-2 DI-pattern study (analysis/tier2_transform) ---
# Raw uvicorn access logs are ~1.8GB (dominated by ciiceronee S1 and azure S1)
# and are provenance only. The per-cell aggregates in raw.tsv are what the
# analysis reads, so the raw logs are never tracked.
analysis/tier2_transform/results/**/server.log
# The four cloned app repos (3.1GB, incl. .git and node_modules) and the
# 24MB tool venv under scripts/ are build inputs, not study artifacts.
analysis/tier2_transform/repos/
analysis/tier2_transform/scripts/.toolenv/
